@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+- Less GPU upload memory on D3D12 and Vulkan. Devices are requested with 8 to 16 MB device blocks (4 to 8 MB host blocks) instead of `MemoryUsage`'s blocks that grow to 64 and 32 MB: an upload block is committed whole while one small staging chunk lives in it. Staging chunks the GPU handed back are freed each frame (`Staging::reclaim`), and a window that goes idle after an upload burst polls the device once so the burst's chunks come back and are freed. `gpu_allocator_report` gives the allocator's last report (blocks, use and the largest allocations), taken at a window's first image upload, when it goes idle and when it goes out of sight.
